   "text": "This is my best reading of the drawing, and I am unsure about two parts. The unspecified N-terminal fragment and all stereocentres other than the drawn Ala are assumed, not read from the image.\n\n**Backbone.** The macrocycle runs, from the free C-terminus around the ring, as: Thr (free COOH) \u2013 Cys \u2013 Trp \u2013 Val \u2013 Leu \u2013 Glu \u2013 Gly \u2013 Leu \u2013 His \u2013 Trp \u2013 Ala \u2013 a Cys-like residue. The side chains match this order: indole, isopropyl, isobutyl, CH2CH2COOH, imidazole, and so on.\n\n**Thioether bridge.** The CH2 of the Cys-like residue is joined through the S atom to the CH2 of the ring Cys, closing the macrocycle. In the SMILES, ring-closure digit 1 sits on the S and on the Cys CH2.\n\n**Unresolved N-terminal fragment.** The Cys-like residue's NH is attached to a wavy bond and a carbon with two truncated lines. I could not tell what this group is, so I modelled it as an isopropyl group on nitrogen, which is a guess.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I assumed natural L-configuration at every \u03b1-carbon, including Thr with its drawn OH, and the Cys-like residue. I did not verify each wedge against the drawing.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)N[C@@H](CS1)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]cn2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](C1)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)O"
